steps.body:
To find the most intervals that overlap at any moment, turn each interval into two **events**: +1 at its start and -1 at its end. Sort the events by time and walk them with a running count. The count only changes at an event, so its biggest value is the answer. With `type Interval struct{ Start, End int }` and `type Event struct{ Time, Delta int }`:

```go harness
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"sort"
)

type Interval struct{ Start, End int }

type Event struct{ Time, Delta int }

func main() {
	{{code}}
}
```

```go
ivs := []Interval{{1, 4}, {2, 5}, {4, 6}}
var events []Event
for _, iv := range ivs {
	events = append(events, Event{iv.Start, 1}, Event{iv.End, -1})
}
sort.Slice(events, func(i, j int) bool {
	if events[i].Time != events[j].Time {
		return events[i].Time < events[j].Time
	}
	return events[i].Delta < events[j].Delta // same time: ends (-1) first
})
count, best := 0, 0
for _, e := range events {
	count += e.Delta
	if count > best {
		best = count
	}
}
fmt.Println(best) // 2
```

The tie-break matters. An interval holds from its start up to its end, so `{1, 4}` is gone at time 4, when `{4, 6}` arrives. With ends first, the count dips from 2 to 1 and back to 2 at time 4. With starts first it would reach 3, for a moment that never happened. When touching intervals should count as overlapping, put the starts first instead.

There are 2n events, so the sort is O(n log n), the walk O(n), and the events take O(n) space.

example.code:
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"sort"
)

type Event struct{ Time, Delta int }

func main() {
	var n int
	fmt.Scan(&n)
	var events []Event
	for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
		var arrive, leave int
		fmt.Scan(&arrive, &leave)
		events = append(events, Event{arrive, 1}, Event{leave, -1})
	}

	sort.Slice(events, func(i, j int) bool {
		if events[i].Time != events[j].Time {
			return events[i].Time < events[j].Time
		}
		return events[i].Delta < events[j].Delta // a car leaves before one arrives
	})

	count, best, bestHour := 0, 0, 0
	for _, e := range events {
		count += e.Delta
		if count > best {
			best, bestHour = count, e.Time
		}
	}
	fmt.Printf("most cars at once: %d, first at hour %d\n", best, bestHour)
}

